==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|naughty}}, {{m|enm|nauȝty}}, {{m|enm|nauȝti}}, {{m|enm|naȝti}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|naught|y}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈnɔːti/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈnɔti/|/ˈnɑti/}}
* {{homophones|en|knotty}} {{qualifier|in accents with the [[w:cot-caught merger|cot-caught merger]]}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-naughty.ogg|Audio (US cot-caught merged)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːti|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# [[mischievous|Mischievous]]; tending to [[misbehave]] or act badly (especially of a child). {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|Some '''naughty''' boys at school hid the teacher's lesson notes.}}
# Sexually provocative; now in weakened sense, [[risqué]], [[cheeky]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|I bought some '''naughty''' lingerie for my honeymoon.}}
#: {{ux|en|If I see you send another '''naughty''' email to your friends, you will be forbidden from using the computer!}}
# {{lb|en|now|_|rare|archaic}} [[evil|Evil]], [[wicked]], morally [[reprehensible]]. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#* '''1589''', John Bucke, ''Instructions for the Use of the Beades''
#*: my proneſſe to ſinne, and '''naughty''' appetites and desires, woulde drawe me headlong to the pitte of hell
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|V|i|text={{...}}How far that little candle throws his beams!<br>So shines a good deed in a '''naughty''' world.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Areopagitica|text=Wholesome meats to a vitiated stomack differ little or nothing from unwholesome; and best books to a '''naughty''' mind are not unappliable to occasions of evill.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[bad|Bad]], [[worthless]], [[substandard]]. {{defdate|16th–19th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author={{w|Andrew Boorde}}|title=The First Boke of the Introduction of Knowledge|year=1542|passage=In Cornwall is two speches, the one is '''naughty''' Englysshe, and the other is Cornysshe speche.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Jeremiah|24|2|passage=One basket had very good figs, even like the figs that are first ripe: and the other basket had very '''naughty''' figs, which could not be eaten, they were so bad.}}

